Error [E0804]: A lambda can't call itself as `f`
  --> tests/ui/lambda_self_recursive.jet:2:10
    |
  2 |     f :: (x: Int) -> {
    |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Short functions stored in a binding can't recurse in v1
 Fix: Write a named `fn` instead of assigning the lambda to `f`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0804

Error [E0107]: Nothing named `f` exists here
  --> tests/ui/lambda_self_recursive.jet:2:10
    |
  2 |     f :: (x: Int) -> {
    |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A name must be declared before it's used
 Fix: Declare it first: `f :: ...`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0107

Error [E0107]: Nothing named `f` exists here
  --> tests/ui/lambda_self_recursive.jet:3:19
    |
  3 |         copy_f :: f
    |                   ^
 Why: A name must be declared before it's used
 Fix: Did you mean `x`?
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0107

Error [E0102]: Nothing named `copy_f` exists here
  --> tests/ui/lambda_self_recursive.jet:4:9
    |
  4 |         copy_f(x - 1)
    |         ^^^^^^
 Why: Only functions that have been defined (or built in, like `print` / `input`) can be called
 Fix: Define it first (fn copy_f() { ... }), or call one that exists
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0102

